.TH NEEDLEFISH 1 "August 2026" "Needlefish 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
needlefish \- high-performance embedded full-text & regex search engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B needlefish
\fIcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBneedlefish\fR is an ultra-fast, zero-copy, memory-mapped full-text search engine implemented in C++20. It combines an inverted index with Block-Max WAND pruning, BitPacking, SIMD acceleration, Burrows-Wheeler Transform FM-Index substring indexing, and Levenshtein automata for fuzzy query evaluation.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B index
Build an index from a JSONL file.
.TP
.B search
Execute BM25, phrase, regex, or fuzzy queries against an existing index.
.TP
.B suggest
Generate prefix and fuzzy autocomplete term suggestions from the index trie.
.TP
.B stats
Display metadata and section breakdown for an index file.
.TP
.B serve
Start the HTTP search API daemon and embedded web search interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " \fIfile.jsonl\fR"
Path to input JSONL file for indexing.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIindex.idx\fR"
Path to output unified index file.
.TP
.BR \-\-index " \fIindex.idx\fR"
Path to existing index file to open.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-query " \fIstring\fR"
Search query string or autocomplete prefix.
.TP
.BR \-k " \fInumber\fR"
Maximum number of top-ranked results to return (default: 10).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fuzzy " [\fIdistance\fR]"
Enable Levenshtein fuzzy matching within edit distance (default: 2, max: 2).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-enable\-fm ", " \-\-enable\-substring
Enable substring FM-index indexing during build or substring matching during search.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-regex
Force evaluation of query as a regular expression.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " \fIport\fR"
Port for HTTP daemon (default: 8080).
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-web\-dir " \fIdirectory\fR"
Path to static web assets directory (default: web).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR grep (1),
.BR sed (1)
